            <ArticleTitle>Clinical applications of oesophageal motility studies?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>267-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Technological advances in the investigation of oesophageal motility have resulted in progressive awareness of gastro-oesophageal reflux disease and motor disorders of the oesophagus as causes of obscure &quot;noncardiac&quot; chest pain, as well as for unexplained swallowing difficulties. Oesophageal motility studies should also be undertaken before surgery for reflux oesophagitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
